Chapter 9 Notes

OOP = Object Oriented Programming
UML = Unified Modeling Language

Objects
- An object represents a real world entity
- An object is an instance of a class. Objects created in main method are instances of their class
- (the word instance emphasizes the relationship between an object and its class, i.e. house blueprint and the house created from blueprint)
- An object has a unique state(date fields) and behavior(methods)

UML
- A UML is a class diagram
- Class name is at the top and centered
- Data fields are written first and then contructors and additional methods are last, these two are seperated with a line
- Visibility modifiers are indentified with "+" "-", and i'll find the other ones later
- A data member is denoted as dataMember: dataMemberType
- A constructor is denoted as ClassName(parameterName: paramaterType)
- A method is denoted as methodName(parameterName: paramaterType): returnType
